    <briefdescription>
<para>Abstract base class for all simulation models in the Weaver framework. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The <computeroutput><ref refid="class_model" kindref="compound">Model</ref></computeroutput> class establishes the interface that all derived simulation models must follow. It encapsulates the essential lifecycle methods (<computeroutput>run</computeroutput>) and provides a static factory method for model creation.</para>
<para>The derived classes (e.g., <computeroutput><ref refid="class_i_b_m" kindref="compound">IBM</ref></computeroutput>) implement specific simulation logic while conforming to this standardized structure.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="par"><title>Responsibilities</title><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Define the contract for simulation execution (<computeroutput>run</computeroutput>).</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Provide a common base for polymorphic use across different model types. </para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
